avformat/hls: apply the X-TIMESTAMP-MAP header of WebVTT segments

Backport of FFmpeg commit b4738344cd by Kacper Michajłow, as committed
upstream; the tests it adds are left out.

Set the timestamp_map option of the webvtt demuxer for the subtitle
segments in place of prefer_hls_mpegts_pts, which no demuxer has, so the
cue times land on the MPEG-TS timeline of the audio and video. That time
is on the 33 bit PES clock, so each cue is put on the period of that clock
nearest to the position of the media, which is read first when both are
enabled. A cue read without any media does not become that position, and
a cue still buffered when the media is enabled is placed relative to it
before it is returned.

